The accepted toolchain already proves an important simplification: the relay has no third-party Go modules, so the byte-affecting dependency set is the pinned repository source, `go.mod`, the Go 1.26.5 compiler/linker/standard library archive, and the four immutable relay outputs. I’m now binding those records to the existing asset manifest with a non-circular shared linkage digest and fail-closed metadata checks.
