.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-apc34w_verify-relux-works-apple-account-readiness/progress.md:44:AUDIT 2026-08-10: Gate P0 account readiness is NOT READY, while the audit deliverable is ready for review. Technical evidence: accepted C1 authenticated Relux Works portal/team authority; Team ID 262RZ595FP; fresh team-scoped Xcode Network Extensions metadata editable/public with no separate distribution approval request; current Relux Works signing identities present. Open blockers: APC34W-B1 organization enrollment type plus active paid-through date (Relux Works Account Holder); B2 current DPLA status (Account Holder); B3 exact Admin role plus Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles grant (Account Holder); B4 enabled registration of privacy-safe Mac ref sha256:8ea3983a9990 and inclusion in four Mac Development profiles (Apple Platform/CI Admin + TASK-260715-3jloqy); B5 unavailable unattended portal observation (Ceremony C1/local automation owner). Physical iPhone is APC34W-G1, deferred under ADR-024, neither pass nor failure, owner TASK-260715-1kntdx. Default Keychain lock made the named-profile read exit 1; TASK-260728-dveo1o owns revalidation. Validation: git diff --check exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; 13 outcome assertions exit 0. Initial privacy classifier exit 1 due invalid quoting and overbroad historical-logbook scope; corrected task-scoped scan found 0 private-key headers, 0 full 40-hex IDs, 0 UUID-shaped IDs, 0 credential assignments, exit 0. Outcome: TASK-260715-apc34w_results.md.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2cjf4i_m2-physical-validation/TASK-260715-2m7lwo_run-macos-udp-and-dns-exit-validation/README.md:7:In scope: supported physical Apple-silicon Mac and macOS; generated development provider; controlled SSH exit; controlled IPv4 and IPv6 UDP echo or application fixtures; domain-destination fixture; approved resolver; dig or equivalent UDP and TCP DNS clients; authorized physical and exit captures; stable Ethernet or Wi-Fi starting path; association and drop counters; memory; relay process evidence; repeated start and stop; redaction. Out of scope: network transitions, sleep or wake, NAT64 transition, captive recovery, degraded-mode transitions, final QUIC policy, notarization, production traffic, legacy product behavior, and unsupported Intel client hardware.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260715-312u2k_record-release-readiness-go-no-go-decision/README.md:10:1. The decision names exact source, relay staging digest, macOS asset digest, iOS App Store Connect build ID, versions, policy and metadata revisions, storefronts, and review-package revision. 2. Every required gate is present, current, passing, and independently verifiable or the decision is hold or reject with exact owner and resume condition. 3. Approved exceptions are scoped, risk accepted by authorized roles, time limited, visible in notes and review materials where relevant, and do not waive Gate A0, P0, signing, privacy, legal, or credential safety. 4. Product, engineering, security, privacy or legal, release, support, and App Review owners record approval according to the contract. 5. The signed decision and evidence index are retained before any production publication or App Review submission and later artifact or metadata change invalidates it.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/progress.md:23:- [x] All up-front signing, notarization, Sparkle, and portal grants are recorded without secrets
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/progress.md:44:C1 started 2026-07-28 on current Apple-silicon Mac. Privacy-safe preflight: login Keychain accessible; Apple Development and Developer ID Application signing identities present; Xcode account metadata present; notarization source context present but no named notarytool profile detected; official Sparkle 2.9.4 release digest verified and generate_keys prepared in an ephemeral directory. No secret value, path, key ID, issuer ID, or credential was recorded. Current authoritative scope is matrix revision 2026-07-28.r12: four macOS App IDs, Network Extensions only, four Mac Development profiles; no App Groups, no Keychain Sharing, no iOS mutation.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/progress.md:45:C1 credential steps completed: temporary codesign probes succeeded for the Relux Works Apple Development identity and Developer ID Application identity using /usr/bin/codesign; no Keychain prompt was required. Named notarytool profile relux-works-notary was stored in login Keychain and validated successfully against the notary service. Official Sparkle 2.9.4 generate_keys completed and stored its private EdDSA key in login Keychain; public output remains ephemeral for the unattended evidence task. Source notarization key disposition remains awaiting explicit owner choice. Apple Developer account page was opened for manual sign-in/2FA confirmation; no portal mutation has begun.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/progress.md:46:OWNER DECISION 2026-08-10: retain the source notarization API private-key file and its owner note. Do not delete, move, rename, inspect, echo, upload, or record their paths or identifiers. They remain owner-controlled recovery material outside repository/board/logs and are not an automation credential; unattended notarization must use only the validated named login-Keychain profile. This explicitly resolves the C1 source-disposition question as retain, not delete.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/progress.md:60:OWNER DECISION 2026-08-10: choose reviewer Option B. Amend AC1, AC2, AC3, AC7 and ADR-028 to accept resumed functional evidence. Preserve the single board-node ownership model and all security/privacy outcomes, but do not require one continuous sitting, contemporaneous proof of the historical Always Allow click, separately timestamped two-factor, or suppression of harmless command names. Effective prompt-free signing access, authenticated Relux Works portal/team authority, named Keychain-backed credentials, honest provenance/deviation reporting, and zero secret values or secret paths in repository, board, logs, and history are the required evidence. This is explicit owner authorization for the precise contract amendment requested by reviewer verdict 01.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/progress.md:65:IMPLEMENTER REWORK 2026-08-10: Applied the owner-selected Option B contract amendment to live AC1/AC2/AC3/AC7, ADR-028, goal/delivery specs, and LOGBOOK. One human ceremony remains one board node; resumed interactions and intervening agent cycles are recorded honestly. Functional signing/portal evidence is accepted without invented Always Allow or two-factor timestamps. Harmless command-name-only history is permitted; zero secret values and secret paths remains mandatory. Gates: r12 matrix 2862 checks exit 0; live A1/P1/D1 consumer gate exit 0; git diff --check exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; corrected forbidden-continuity scan exit 0; post-amendment privacy scan exit 0 with zero candidates. An earlier overbroad continuity classifier exited 1 by counting clauses that prohibit an uninterrupted-session claim; it is recorded in the outcome and not represented as passing.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/README.md:1:# TASK-260717-ziprhs: generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/README.md:4:Record the Sparkle EdDSA update-signing key evidence and custody. The ed25519 keypair is generated and the PRIVATE key is placed into approved custody once inside Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta), alongside the Developer ID and notarization credentials. This task runs unattended afterwards and records the PUBLIC key, its fingerprint, the tool version, the generation date, and the custody location by name only, plus the rotation and revocation procedure. It deliberately stops there: pinning SUPublicEDKey, wiring the CI signing secret, and verifying a signed appcast are owned by TASK-260728-3bj9bk, because the generated macOS target, the updater integration, and the appcast pipeline do not exist yet. Completing this task does not mean self-update signing works.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/README.md:7:In scope: verifying that the keypair generated at Ceremony C1 exists and that the private key resides only in the approved custody store; recording the public key, its fingerprint, the pinned Sparkle vendor tool version, and the generation date as non-secret evidence; the rotation and revocation procedure for this keypair; a leak scan. Out of scope: generating the keypair or moving the private key (TASK-260728-q5kjta owns the ceremony); editing any Info.plist or project manifest; creating or binding CI secrets; signing or verifying an appcast; publishing release assets; any claim that the updater integration or CI signing path is complete.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260717-ziprhs_generate-and-install-sparkle-eddsa-update-signing-secret/README.md:10:1. The keypair generated at Ceremony C1 is confirmed present and the pinned Sparkle vendor tool version and generation date are recorded. 2. The private key resides only in the approved custody store; it is absent from git, board resources, shell history, and logs, and its bytes are never echoed. 3. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records the public key value and fingerprint, the custody location by name only, and the rotation and revocation procedure. 4. The outcome states explicitly that SUPublicEDKey pinning and appcast signing verification remain open under TASK-260728-3bj9bk and are not evidenced here. 5. A post-run scan of the repository, board resources, and run logs finds no private key material.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260715-8g5fpa_configure-app-store-connect-and-ios-distribution-environment/README.md:10:1. Every certificate, profile, issuer credential, App Store Connect role, agreement, and environment reviewer has an accountable owner, minimum scope, expiry or review date, rotation, and revocation path. 2. Trusted jobs import signing material into an ephemeral keychain, validate key and certificate match, Team ID, profile IDs, bundle coverage, entitlements, expiry, and App Store Connect app access, then clean up on all exits. 3. Upload or build-management credentials cannot manage unrelated apps or access account functions not required by the workflow where App Store Connect permits scoping. 4. Forks, pull requests, unapproved branches, ordinary runners, logs, caches, and retained artifacts cannot access certificate keys, issuer keys, profiles containing sensitive metadata, or sessions. 5. Dry runs cover valid, missing, expired, revoked, wrong-team, wrong-bundle, wrong-role, unsigned-agreement, masked-log, cancellation, rotation, and emergency-revocation cases.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/README.md:4:Prove and record the Keychain-only notarization custody required by ADR-025 before any notarization step is declared ready. The interactive notarytool store-credentials run and the owner disposition decision for the source App Store Connect API private-key file happen once inside Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta). This task runs unattended afterwards: it verifies that the NAMED Keychain profile authenticates against the real Apple notary service using only its name, records the non-secret evidence and the disposition the owner chose, defines rotation and revocation, and scans for leaks. The agent never receives, echoes, or persists secret values.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/README.md:7:In scope: a read-only notary history or whoami style authentication check performed with the named login-Keychain profile alone; recording the profile name, the fact a profile exists, the authenticating team identifier, and the check outcome; transcribing the owner-approved disposition chosen at C1 for the source .p8 file from Keychain-backed migration, retention under a named custodian with documented access control, or secure destruction, and verifying that the stated disposition actually holds; a repeatable rotation and revocation procedure keyed to the profile name; shell-history and command-echo suppression plus a post-run leak scan. Out of scope: performing the interactive store-credentials or making the disposition decision (TASK-260728-q5kjta owns both); recording or transmitting the source file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes anywhere; submitting a real notarization of a product artifact; configuring CI notarization secrets (TASK-260715-3gkwn0 owns the separately-scoped CI credential); Developer ID certificate issuance; iOS or App Store Connect distribution credentials.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/README.md:10:1. A read-only authentication check succeeds using only the named notarytool Keychain profile, with the command transcript showing no secret value. 2. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records the profile name, the authenticating team identifier, the check outcome, the date, and the rotation/revocation procedure; it records no file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes. 3. The owner-approved disposition of the source App Store Connect API private-key file chosen at Ceremony C1 is transcribed and independently verified to hold; a mode-0600 file left in place with no recorded custodian is an explicit fail. 4. Shell history and command echo are suppressed for every command, and a post-run scan of the repository, board resources, shell history, and run logs finds no notarization secret material. 5. If the profile is absent, fails to authenticate, or the disposition was not decided at C1, the task records the exact blocking input needed and remains blocked rather than reporting a ready notarization path.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/progress.md:26:The gap: the owner readiness record states the notarization credential exists as a mode-0600 .p8 file. No existing board element owned bringing it into the Keychain-only form the invariant demands. TASK-260715-3gkwn0 owns the CI release environment, not local credential custody, and its AC assumes a usable credential already exists.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2byjks_m5-release-gates-and-ceremonies/TASK-260728-dveo1o_establish-notarytool-keychain-credential-custody/progress.md:27:Out-of-scope check before creation: searched STORY-260716-2byjks and STORY-260716-2m2tl1 for an existing notarization-custody task - none. 3gkwn0 explicitly scopes out local Keychain custody. No duplicate created.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/README.md:7:In scope under the resumed-evidence amendment, within this one ceremony node: establishing effective prompt-free private-key access for the Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities to the signing tools that run unattended; confirming an authenticated Xcode or Apple Developer portal context for the Relux Works team and the exact macOS-only matrix authority, while honestly recording whether a separate two-factor timestamp exists and any later reauthentication risk; authorizing creation and download of exactly the macOS entries in the approved identifier and entitlement matrix (revision 2026-07-28.r12) and nothing beyond them, namely the four macOS App IDs works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel, the Network Extensions capability on those four and no other capability, and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered as a device; explicitly NOT creating any App Group record, NOT enabling the App Groups capability on any App ID, and NOT performing any Keychain access group mutation, because matrix rule G4 prohibits com.apple.security.application-groups on every macOS target, rule K2 prohibits keychain-access-groups on every macOS target, and keychain sharing has no portal record at all; storing a NAMED notarytool profile in the login Keychain; choosing and stating the owner disposition for the source App Store Connect API private-key file; generating the Sparkle ed25519 keypair with the pinned vendor tool and placing the private key into approved custody; recording only non-secret grant facts and honest provenance. Harmless command-name-only shell history is permitted, but secret values, secret-bearing arguments, identifiers, account credentials, key bytes, and secret paths are prohibited everywhere. Out of scope: approving any system VPN or system extension dialog (that is Approval A1 and later Hold H2, and no signed artifact exists yet); provisioning the deferred iOS identifiers; creating any Developer ID or App Store distribution profile; performing the portal mutations themselves (TASK-260715-3jloqy); validating profiles, verifying notary authentication, or recording public-key evidence (owned by the downstream evidence tasks); any product code; any owner product decision.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260728-q5kjta_conduct-c1-apple-permission-ceremony/README.md:10:1. Ceremony C1 remains exactly one up-front human-input board node. Evidence may be collected across resumed owner interactions with producer or reviewer cycles between them, provided the record gives every known interaction date or time, states which boundaries were not captured, identifies the intervening cycles, and makes no uninterrupted-session claim. The human is never asked to remain present through a producer or reviewer cycle. 2. Effective prompt-free private-key access is demonstrated for the Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities to the named unattended signing tools. The record names the identities by common name and the tools, never key material. Contemporaneous proof of the historical Always Allow click is not required; any provenance limitation is stated honestly. 3. An authenticated Xcode or Apple Developer portal context for the Relux Works team exists and the operator has confirmed authority to create the macOS entries in the approved matrix. A cached authenticated session is acceptable functional evidence without a separately timestamped two-factor event; the record states that limitation and any residual fresh-authentication or two-factor interaction the portal may force later. 4. Creation and download of exactly the approved macOS entries is authorized and nothing beyond them: the four macOS App IDs works.relux.tunnel.mac, works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac and works.relux.tunnel.probe.mac.tunnel; the Network Extensions capability on those four; and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Mac registered. The record states explicitly that NO App Group record was created, that the App Groups capability was enabled on no App ID, that no Keychain access group portal mutation was performed or required, and that no Developer ID or App Store distribution profile was created. All FOUR iOS App IDs (works.relux.tunnel.ios, works.relux.tunnel.ios.tunnel, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios, works.relux.tunnel.probe.ios.tunnel) are explicitly NOT authorized because iOS is deferred under ADR-024, and works.relux.proxy is not touched. 5. A NAMED notarytool credential profile is stored in the login Keychain and the owner states the disposition for the source App Store Connect API private-key file; only the profile name and the chosen disposition are recorded, never the file path, key ID, issuer ID, passphrase, or key bytes. 6. The Sparkle ed25519 keypair is generated with the pinned vendor tool and the private key is placed in approved custody; only the custody location name is recorded here. 7. Credential values and secret-bearing arguments are never echoed or recorded. A post-ceremony scan of the repository, board resources, run logs, and shell history finds no secret value, secret path, key ID, issuer ID, account credential, or key bytes. Harmless command-name-only history is permitted and must be reported honestly rather than suppressed from the evidence. 8. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome records which grants succeeded, which were declined, honest interaction provenance, and any residual interaction the portal may still force later; a declined grant is recorded as a named blocker on the specific downstream task rather than as an assumed grant.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-9yp8to_verify-p0-on-physical-apple-silicon-mac/README.md:4:Install and exercise the disposable macOS probe on the designated Apple-silicon Mac. Capture a repeatable end-to-end record of nested signing, VPN configuration, provider launch, app messaging, system approval behavior, repeated stop, and clean reinstall.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-9yp8to_verify-p0-on-physical-apple-silicon-mac/README.md:7:In scope: physical Apple-silicon Mac and current supported macOS; development-signed host and embedded provider; nested signature and entitlement inspection; system VPN approval; manager save and reload; launch, message, stop, host termination, uninstall and reinstall; privacy-safe unified logs. Out of scope: Intel-only evidence, Developer ID release, notarization, DMG publication, packet forwarding, and changing the shipped SwiftPM application.
.task-board/EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2m2tl1_m0-viability-manual-gates/TASK-260715-9yp8to_verify-p0-on-physical-apple-silicon-mac/README.md:10:1. Evidence records Mac model, exact macOS and Xcode, source revision, profile metadata, bundle versions, signing identity class, and test timestamp without private credentials. 2. Inside-out nested signature, designated requirement, embedded profile, and entitlement inspections all match the approved matrix. 3. The app saves and reloads one manager, starts the provider, receives the expected versioned message, and stops cleanly after required system approval. 4. At least ten start and stop cycles plus host termination and reinstall show no stale manager duplication, orphaned provider, crash, or unexplained launch failure. 5. A TASK-ID-scoped runbook and redacted result bundle supports repetition by another authorized operator.

