+# TASK-260715-vtot05 — developer handoff evidence
+
+Date: 2026-08-19
+Disposition: ready for review
+
+## Delivered
+
+- Added `relay/supply-chain-source-v1.json` as the authoritative relay-only metadata contract. It pins the accepted relay Git commit, repository/relay tree IDs, every compiled repository file SHA-256, the standard-library-only `go.mod`, the historical build-recipe revision/files, exact build command and targets, Go 1.26.5 compiler/internal-linker archive, explicit no-container base-image boundary, component licenses, notice obligations, and runtime no-code-download policy.
+- Deterministically generated `relay/dependency-inventory-v1.json`, `relay/source-build-provenance-v1.json`, and `relay/PRODUCT_NOTICES.txt`. The inventory is the scoped vulnerability-review input; it is not represented as the final product-wide SBOM.
+- Extended the exact four-asset manifest/schema/Swift catalog with source provenance, inventory, and notice hashes. A shared linkage SHA-256 covers the manifest schema, source/recipe/toolchain inputs, accepted archive, and ordered asset sizes/hashes without a circular file-hash dependency.
+- Added fail-closed `make relay-supply-chain-audit`, generation, and test commands plus CI integration. Negative tests cover missing dependency metadata, mutable URLs, missing notice coverage, linkage drift, and runtime code-download surfaces.
+- Recorded the ownership boundary in machine-readable metadata and `docs/relay-supply-chain.md`: M2 owns source pinning/reproducibility/assets/notices; M5 signing is `TASK-260715-3sk5cd`, notarization is `TASK-260715-387eof`, release attestation is `TASK-260715-1gzhnk`, and distribution approval is `TASK-260715-312u2k`.
+
+## Output SHA-256
+
+- Supply-chain source: `3381e117be383b0606c9a1530f0b7a8b0fdf2c6057c5370172de31f31c2a84bc`
+- Scoped inventory: `6de15981862301fcc7a5ece451039f7d4b892e7a33a56c727d3597eb09a8f956`
+- Source/build provenance: `c453c793cf02e951ac5cc66a7f3e852ff0a2a3a6d75a08718d4c95b12dce7233`
+- Product notice input: `7f1edb1216363e034bd06b4d41edfd04958a597b0dad8ae3cdd4e7c91c69006f`
+- Asset source contract: `b5229505ce1e7d50c47db0ed645ca3fac249c4f6270bc08eb667a1350bf91a3b`
+
+## Validation
+
+- `make relay-supply-chain-audit relay-supply-chain-test relay-asset-manifest-test`: exit 0; clean audit passed, 8 supply-chain tests passed, 26 asset-manifest Python tests passed, and 4 Swift manifest tests passed.
+- `make relay-shell-test relay-shell-vet`: exit 0; all relay Go packages passed, 35 release-tool tests passed, and Go vet passed under the pinned offline toolchain.
+- `swift build`: exit 0.
+- Python compilation, Black check, Swift format lint, Actionlint, JSON parsing, and `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- Two consecutive `make relay-supply-chain-generate` runs produced byte-identical hashes for all generated metadata and Swift linkage: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate`: exit 0 but reports `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` because the task/story is in development while `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` remains backlog. An explicit parent repair attempt exited 1 because unfinished dependencies `EPIC-260715-2mqgvm` and `EPIC-260715-3810we` prohibit the epic's development transition. No validation or supply-chain gate was weakened.
+
+## Safety
+
+No signing, notarization, attestation, publishing, app/provider installation or launch, VPN preference mutation, tunnel activation, route/interface/firewall/DNS change, credential lookup, or network fetch was performed. Generated artifacts contain repository-relative paths only and passed sensitive/workstation-data checks.
