+# TASK-260715-vtot05 — developer handoff evidence
+
+Date: 2026-08-19
+Disposition: ready for review
+
+## Delivered
+
+- Added `relay/supply-chain-source-v1.json` as the authoritative relay-only metadata contract. It pins the accepted relay Git commit, repository/relay tree IDs, every compiled repository file SHA-256, the standard-library-only `go.mod`, the historical build-recipe revision/files, exact build command and targets, Go 1.26.5 compiler/internal-linker archive, explicit no-container base-image boundary, component licenses, notice obligations, and runtime no-code-download policy.
+- Deterministically generated `relay/dependency-inventory-v1.json`, `relay/source-build-provenance-v1.json`, and `relay/PRODUCT_NOTICES.txt`. The inventory is the scoped vulnerability-review input; it is not represented as the final product-wide SBOM.
+- Extended the exact four-asset manifest/schema/Swift catalog with source provenance, inventory, and notice hashes. A shared linkage SHA-256 covers the manifest schema, source/recipe/toolchain inputs, accepted archive, and ordered asset sizes/hashes without a circular file-hash dependency.
+- Added fail-closed `make relay-supply-chain-audit`, generation, and test commands plus CI integration. Negative tests cover missing dependency metadata, mutable URLs, missing notice coverage, linkage drift, and runtime code-download surfaces.
+- Recorded the ownership boundary in machine-readable metadata and `docs/relay-supply-chain.md`: M2 owns source pinning/reproducibility/assets/notices; M5 signing is `TASK-260715-3sk5cd`, notarization is `TASK-260715-387eof`, release attestation is `TASK-260715-1gzhnk`, and distribution approval is `TASK-260715-312u2k`.
+
